#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:178
msgid "Hardened RHEL environments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:180
msgid ""
"When deploying Mattermost on hardened RHEL systems, additional security "
"configurations may be required. Select the tab below for your specific "
"security tool:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:185
msgid ""
"When deploying Mattermost from RHEL9, which has SELinux running with "
"enforcing mode enabled by default, additional configuration is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:187
msgid ""
"SELinux is a security module that provides access control security "
"policies. It's enabled by default on RHEL and CentOS systems. SELinux can"
" block access to files, directories, and ports, which can cause issues "
"when starting Mattermost. To resolve these issues, you'll need to set the"
" appropriate SELinux contexts for the Mattermost binaries and "
"directories, and allow Mattermost to bind to ports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:189
msgid ""
"Ensure that SELinux is enabled and in enforcing mode by running the "
"``sestatus`` command. If it's ``enforcing``, you'll need to configure it "
"properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:192
msgid "Set bin contexts for /opt/mattermost/bin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:194
msgid ""
"SELinux enforces security contexts for binaries. To label the Mattermost "
"binaries as safe, you'll need to set them to the below SELinux context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:201
msgid "Now, try starting Mattermost again with"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:207
msgid ""
"If you don't receive an error, verify that Mattermost is running: curl "
"``http://localhost:8065``. You should see the HTML that's returned by the"
" Mattermost Server. You're all set!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:209
msgid ""
"If on starting Mattermost you receive an error, before moving on, check "
"for the existence of a file in ``/opt/mattermost/logs`` - if "
"``mattermost.log`` exists in that directory, it's more likely you're "
"dealing with a configuration issue in ``config.json``. Double check the "
"previous steps before continuing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:212
msgid "Try different contexts for /opt/mattermost"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:214
msgid ""
"SELinux enforces security contexts for files and directories. To label "
"your Mattermost directory as safe, you'll need to set an appropriate "
"SELinux context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:216
msgid ""
"Check current context by running ``ls -Z /opt/mattermost``. When you see "
"something like ``drwxr-xr-x. root root unconfined_u:object_r:default_t:s0"
" mattermost`` returned, the ``default_t`` indicates that SELinux doesn't "
"know what this directory is for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:217
msgid ""
"Set a safe context by assigning a SELinux type that's compatible with web"
" services or applications by running ``sudo semanage fcontext -a -t "
"httpd_sys_content_t \"/opt/mattermost(/.*)?\"``. A common one is "
"``httpd_sys_content_t``, used for serving files. Ensure you match the "
"directory and its contents recursively. Run the ``sudo restorecon -R "
"/opt/mattermost`` to apply the changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:220
msgid "Allow Mattermost to bind to ports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:222
msgid ""
"When Mattermost needs specific ports (e.g., 8065), ensure that SELinux "
"allows it by allowing Mattermost to bind to ports. Run the ``sudo "
"semanage port -l | grep 8065`` command, and if the port's not listed, "
"you'll need to add it by running ``sudo semanage port -a -t http_port_t "
"-p tcp 8065``, replacing the ``8065`` with the required port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:225
msgid "Handle custom policies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:227
msgid ""
"If Mattermost requires actions that SELinux blocks, you'll need to "
"generate a custom policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:229
msgid ""
"Check for SELinux denials first in the logs by running ``sudo ausearch -m"
" avc -ts recent``, or by checking the audit log: ``sudo cat "
"/var/log/audit/audit.log | grep denied``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:231
msgid ""
"If needed, generate a policy module by installing ``audit2allow`` to "
"generate policies automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:240
msgid "Test the configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:242
msgid ""
"Restart Mattermost to confirm the configuation works as expected by "
"running ``sudo systemctl restart mattermost``. In the case of failures, "
"revisit the logs to identify other SELinux-related issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:245
msgid "Need Mattermost working quickly for testing purposes?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:247
msgid ""
"You can change SELinux to permissive mode by running the ``sudo "
"setenforce 0``. command where policies aren't enforced, only logged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:248
msgid ""
"This command changes the SELinux mode to \"permissive\". While in "
"permissive mode, policies aren't enforced, and violations are logged "
"instead of being blocked. This can be helpful for debugging and "
"troubleshooting issues related to SELinux policies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/deployment-guide/server/linux/deploy-rhel.rst:249
msgid ""
"Ensure you re-enable enforcing mode once context is working as needed by "
"running the ``sudo setenforce 1`` command."
msgstr ""

